  "step_2": "The individual considers the probabilities of the two lotteries to be very similar (‘die Wahrscheinlichkeiten zwischen Lotteri A und B sehr ähnlich waren’). Based on this, they state they decided in favor of the higher potential gain (‘hab ich mich für den höheren Gewinn entschieden’). The individual explicitly focuses on the magnitude of the favorable outcome (2500 vs. 2400) and notes that the probabilities are nearly identical. Their justification is based on choosing the higher monetary outcome, not on the distribution of probabilities or skewness. They do not mention or consider the relative probability mass on favorable outcomes or the concept of skewness.",
  "step_3": "The decision reason requires evaluating skewness based on the relative probability mass assigned to favorable outcomes. The individual did not consider skewness or the distribution of probabilities in a comparative way; instead, they focused on the absolute difference in the maximum prize. Although the reason would prefer Lottery B (due to slightly higher probability on the favorable outcome), the individual’s justification is based on the higher nominal reward (2500), which suggests they preferred Lottery A. This contradicts the reason’s preference (which favors B). The information considered by the individual (similar probabilities, higher reward) does not align with the skewness-based rule, and their justification does not reference skewness or probability distribution. Therefore, the individual did not use the skewness-based reason to make the decision. However, the individual did acknowledge the similarity in probabilities, which is tangentially related. Still, the core criterion of the reason (skewness) was not invoked. The assessment is not fully certain due to the possibility of implicit consideration, but the explicit justification is inconsistent with the reason. Thus, the reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 10
}

